<article class="env-lemma" id="0FAZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FAZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0FAZ">42.49.8</span>.</a> In Lemma <a href="/tag/0F9K" data-tag="0F9K">42.49.1</a> assume $Q|_ T$ is zero. Assume we have another perfect object $Q' \in D(\mathcal{O}_ W)$ whose Chern classes are defined such that the restriction $Q'|_ T$ is zero. In this case the classes $P'_ p(Q), P'_ p(Q'), P'_ p(Q \oplus Q') \in A^ p(Z \to X)$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0F9K" data-tag="0F9K">42.49.1</a> satisfy $P'_ p(Q \oplus Q') = P'_ p(Q) + P'_ p(Q')$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from the construction of these classes and Lemma <a href="/tag/0FAM" data-tag="0FAM">42.47.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>